\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N$, $\mathbb Z$, $\mathbb Q$, $\mathbb R$, and $\mathbb C$ denote the natural numbers, integers, rationals, reals, and complex numbers, respectively. All additional parameters and hypotheses are specified in the question.


\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Establish, in some energy range, the existence of extended eigenstates or continuous spectrum for linear operators with extensive disorder, such as a discrete Schrödinger operator with an i.i.d. random potential acting on $\ell^2(\mathbb{Z}^d)$. Also clarify the borderline case $d=2$.
\par\smallskip\textit{Formulation references:} \href{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}{[S1]}, \href{https://web.math.princeton.edu/~aizenman/OpenProblems_MathPhys/9809.ExtStates.html}{[S2]}.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Establish, in some energy range, the existence of extended eigenstates or continuous spectrum for linear operators with extensive disorder, such as a discrete Schrödinger operator with an i.i.d. random potential acting on $\ell^2(\mathbb{Z}^d)$. Also clarify the borderline case $d=2$.

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] ULAM.AI and the UnsolvedMath Contributors, UnsolvedMath: A Curated Collection of Open Mathematics Problems, record 7800005 (AMR-077-0005). Catalogue attribution under CC BY 4.0.
\url{https://huggingface.co/datasets/ulamai/UnsolvedMath}.
\item[S2] Original problem formulation and mathematical context.
\url{https://web.math.princeton.edu/~aizenman/OpenProblems_MathPhys/9809.ExtStates.html}.
\end{itemize}
\label{end:7800005}

